s 22 years of the long-term trend. Without El Niño, a Mar–May this warm would come about once every 49 years. Mar–May rainfall has risen by about 5% per decade, with no clear El Niño link. Relative humidity has fallen by about 0.4 points per decade, roughly 3 points since 1951; because warmer air holds more moisture, this does not necessarily mean the air is drier. For Mar–May 2027, a warmer-than-normal season is very likely (more than 95% chance), about 1 °C above the 1991–2020 average; a less humid season than normal is likely (about 75% chance), mostly because of the long-term trend rather than El Niño. This outlook is based on the El Niño strength expected for Sep–Nov 2026 and will be updated when it is observed in early December.","variables":{"temperature":{"normal_1991_2020":27.2549,"trend_per_decade":0.2203,"trend_p":0.0,"trend_total_since_1951":1.6523,"enso_effect_per_degC":0.2188,"enso_p":0.0,"confidence":"Strong","survives_fdr":true,"fraction_explained":0.4308,"intrinsic_sd":0.2357,"effect_this_season":0.4813,"effect_ratio":2.0422,"size":"Dominant","size_typical_el_nino":"Dominant","once_every_n_years_without_el_nino":49.0,"expected_anomaly_2027":0.9539,"p_below":0.0,"p_near":0.0017,"p_above":0.9983,"forecast_words":"Very likely (>95%): a warmer-than-normal season","within_record":true,"years_of_warming_equivalent":21.8447,"values":[26.167,26.504,26.3,26.106,26.3,26.223,26.115,26.725,26.364,26.544,26.728,26.407,26.544,26.6,26.067,26.498,26.054,26.177,26.655,26.66,26.323,26.247,26.783,26.207,26.36,26.431,26.378,26.792,26.858,26.756,26.495,26.463,27.744,26.306,26.513,26.488,26.715,27.047,26.433,27.129,26.715,26.899,26.724,26.638,26.931,26.752,26.899,27.918,26.983,27.043,27.083,27.248,27.352,27.452,27.479,27.271,27.001,26.691,27.219,27.792,27.09,27.046,27.64,27.491,27.328,28.114,27.458,27.472,27.94,27.98,27.312,27.638,27.51,28.218,27.305],"forecast_mean":28.2088,"forecast_sd":0.2582,"fit":{"a2027":27.7275,"b":0.2188,"c":0.022,"tercile_low":27.0293,"tercile_h